      "reason": "The official rule body is the analyzer's IgnoreValidator post-pass (needs the complete diagnostic set of a location); dartq mounts the spec not_dispatched until an engine post-pass exists. Oracle reports 1 row per file; the dartq leg is structurally silent (0 rows enforced here). A dartq UNNECESSARY_IGNORE row in lib/test.g.dart additionally reds the gate by design (the generated-file parity probe, README family 3)."
    },
    {
      "family": "remove_deprecations_in_breaking_versions",
      "files": ["packages/version_breaking/lib/remove_deprecations_in_breaking_versions.dart"],
      "reason": "Registration is gated on the containing package's pubspec version (the pubspec family's mounting seam). The breaking twin fires 2 rows on the oracle leg and stays structurally silent on the dartq leg; the no-version root control and the non-breaking twin are 0 rows on both legs."
